Build option MESEN_EXPANSION_EPSM: the host can plug the EPSM in for a
cartridge whose header does not ask for it.

Mesen plugs the EPSM (a YMF288 on the Famicom's expansion port) in only
when the cartridge's header is NES 2.0 with console type 3 and extended
console type 4. A file with a plain iNES header has no way to say it, and
Mesen's answer is to edit the header (its NES header editor). With this
option the host sets MesenExpansionEpsm before the game is loaded, as a
setting of its own, and the mapper then builds the EPSM as for such a
header. Off, nothing changes.

--- a/Core/NES/BaseMapper.cpp
+++ b/Core/NES/BaseMapper.cpp
@@ -18,6 +18,10 @@
 #include "Utilities/Serializer.h"
 #include "Shared/MemoryType.h"
 #include "Shared/MemoryOperationType.h"
+
+#ifdef MESEN_EXPANSION_EPSM
+bool MesenExpansionEpsm = false;
+#endif
 #include "Shared/FirmwareHelper.h"
 
 void BaseMapper::WriteRegister(uint16_t addr, uint8_t value)
@@ -762,6 +766,13 @@
 
 	_romInfo.HasChrRam = HasChrRam();
 
+#ifdef MESEN_EXPANSION_EPSM
+	//An EPSM the host put in the expansion port, whatever the header says
+	if(MesenExpansionEpsm) {
+		_romInfo.HasEpsm = true;
+	}
+#endif
+
 	if(_romInfo.HasEpsm) {
 		vector<uint8_t> adpcmRom;
 		FirmwareHelper::LoadYmf288AdpcmRom(_emu, adpcmRom);
--- a/Core/NES/BaseMapper.h
